.git
# Don't exclude .agents — internal/features/TestRegistryFilesExist verifies
# the on-disk skill registry under .agents/ycode/skills/ at repo root.
.ycode
.gfy-out
bin/
dist/
priorart/
examples/
*.exe

# HOST-BUILT, PLATFORM-SPECIFIC ARTIFACT — must not enter the Linux image.
#
# ycode-spawn.gz is an untracked build artifact produced by `make
# spawn-embed` for whatever platform you are on, and the Makefile turns on
# the `embed_spawn` build tag CONDITIONALLY on the file existing
# ($(wildcard ...) in TAG_LIST). So a mac-built shim copied into the CI
# image flips the tag on and TestSpawnerShimDispatch dies with
# "exec format error" — a Mach-O binary cannot exec under Linux.
#
# GitHub Actions never sees this: a fresh checkout has no artifact, the tag
# stays off, and the test takes its soft-skip path. Excluding it is what
# makes this image actually mirror CI instead of inheriting the host.
internal/runtime/wrap/spawn_embed/ycode-spawn.gz

# Local agent scratch — never part of a build, and pure cache churn for
# layer invalidation. (.agents itself is deliberately NOT excluded above:
# TestRegistryFilesExist reads the skill registry under it.)
.agents/ycode/memory/
.agents/ycode/qacache/
.aider.tags.cache.v4/
